# Confirmation by sequential test (Wald 1947): each report adds the
# log-likelihood ratio of "same object" against "different objects" to the
# pair, from the difference of the two tracks' full states (position and
# velocity per axis, height when both report it; Bar-Shalom 1981). A pair is
# confirmed when the ratio reaches ln((1 - missed) / false) and released when
# it falls to ln(missed / (1 - false)).
# Derived values:
# - false = missed = 0.01: one wrong pairing, and one missed pairing, per
#   hundred decisions.
# - "different objects" spread pos_m = 10000 m, vel_ms = 300 m/s: other
#   objects lie anywhere within the surveyed area (10 km) and fly at up to
#   300 m/s.
# - height error 100 m per track (hae_sigma_m).
# - gate 9.21: a pair starts a test only inside the 99 % region (chi-square,
#   2 degrees of freedom) of the position difference.
# - stale after 5 times the source's median update interval (last 9), within
#   5 s and 60 s.
# - output fused: the members' estimates weighted by their information, so
#   the output does not depend on source names.
pack           correlate-sprt
version        1.0.0
filter         accel_var=1 default_ce_m=50 vel_sigma_ms=5 unknown_vel_ms=100
maneuver       accel_var=400 p_enter=0.05 p_leave=0.1
gate           mahalanobis gate=9.21
gate           same key=track.simulated
gate           same key=@env
sprt           false=0.01 missed=0.01 pos_m=10000 vel_ms=300 hae_sigma_m=100
stale_rate     factor=5 floor_ms=5000 ceiling_ms=60000 samples=9
same_source    forbid
output         fused
